ds: 8\n- Tens: 8\n- Ones: 9\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5 + 9 = 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 8 = 13, plus 1 is 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 8 = 13, plus 1 is 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 4 + 2 = 6, plus 1 is 7 \u2192 7, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 6 = 9 \u2192 9.\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 4 = 9 \u2192 9.\n\nSo combining all the digits: 997,444? Wait, but when I add 534,555 and 462,889, that seems plausible? Let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding them as whole numbers:\n\n534,555 + 462,889.\n\nLet me add 500,000 + 400,000 = 900,000.\n\nThen 34,555 + 62,889. Wait, 34,555 + 60,000 is 94,555, plus 2,889 is 97,444. So total is 900,000 + 97,444 = 997,444. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 997,444. But let me check once more step by step.\n\nWait, in the thousands place, the original numbers: 534,555 has 4 in the thousands place (since it's 5 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands)), and 462,889 has 2 in the thousands place. So 4 + 2 = 6, plus the carryover 1 makes 7. That's correct. Then ten-thousands: 3 +6 =9, and hundred-thousands 5+4=9. So yes, 997,444. Alright, that seems right.\n</think>\n\n",
