      "text": "\nOkay, let's tackle this addition problem step by step. The question is asking for the sum of 994,737 and 136,202. Hmm, I need to make sure I add each digit correctly, starting from the rightmost ones place and moving left. Let me write them down one above the other to align the digits properly.\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers:\n\n```\n  994737\n+ 136202\n---------\n```\n\nStarting with the ones place: the rightmost digits are 7 and 2. Adding those gives 7 + 2 = 9. That's straightforward, no carrying over needed here.\n\nNext, the tens place: the digits are 3 and 0. 3 + 0 = 3. So the tens place in the sum is 3.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 7 and 2. 7 + 2 equals 9. Easy, so the hundreds digit is 9.\n\nNow the thousands place: 4 and 6. Wait, 4 + 6 is 10. Oh, here we go, that's a two-digit number. I need to write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place. The original digits here are 9 and 3. But don't forget the carried-over 1. So adding them up: 9 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 13. So we put 3 in the ten thousands place and carry over another 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 9 (from the first number) and 1 (from the second number). Adding those gives 10, plus the carried-over 1 makes 11. So that's 1 in the hundred thousands place and another carryover of 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the new digit in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the ones: 9, then 3, 9, 0 (with the carried 1), then 3, 1 (from the ten thousands), and finally the 1 in the millions. Wait, let me check that again to make sure I didn't mix up the places.\n\nWait, maybe I should write each step more carefully:\n\nLet me break it down digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1. Ones place: 7 + 2 = 9\n2. Tens place: 3 + 0 = 3\n3. Hundreds place: 7 + 2 = 9\n4. Thousands place: 4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n5. Ten thousands place: 9 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 13 \u2192 write 3, carryover 1\n6. Hundred thousands place: 9 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n7. Millions place: The carryover 1, since there are no more digits.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left: 1 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (ones). Wait, that would be 1,130,939? Let me verify that.\n\nWait, let me add them numerically:\n\n994,737\n+136,202\n= ?\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n994,737\n+136,202\nLet's add the numbers step by step:\n\nFirst, 994,737 + 100,000 = 1,094,737\n\nThen add 36,202: 1,094,737 + 36,202 = ?\n\n1,094,737 + 30,000 = 1,124,737\n\nThen +6,202: 1,124,737 + 6,202 = 1,130,939. Okay, that matches the previous result. So the total is 1,130,939.\n\nWait, but let me check the digit-by-digit addition again to ensure no mistakes. Let's write each digit's place:\n\nLet me write both numbers with their digits separated:\n\nFirst number: 9 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 7 + 2 = 9\n\nTens: 3 + 0 = 3\n\nHundreds:7 + 2 =9\n\nThousands:4 +6 =10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1\n\nTen thousands:9 +3 =12, plus the carryover 1 makes 13 \u2192 3 with carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands:9 +1 =10, plus carryover 1 makes 11 \u2192 1 with carryover 1\n\nMillions: the carryover 1.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 0 (thousand), 9 (hundred), 3 (ten), 9 (one). So 1,130,939. That's correct.\n\nHmm, so the answer should be 1,130,939. Let me confirm once more with another method. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts:\n\n994,737 can be 900,000 + 94,737\n\n136,202 is 100,000 + 36,202\n\nAdding 900,000 + 100,000 = 1,000,000\n\nThen 94,737 + 36,202 = ?\n\n94,737 + 30,000 = 124,737\n\n124,737 +6,202 = 130,939\n\nThen total is 1,000,