ep with the carryover properly noted.\n\nLet me write it out vertically again, aligning each digit:\n\n        4 0 5 0 1 6\n      +7 6 0 2 6 2\n      -------------\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n6 + 2 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nTens place: 1 + 6 = 7. Write down 7.\n\nHundreds place: 0 + 2 = 2. Write 2.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 0 = 5. Write 5.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 + 6 = 6. Write 6.\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 + 7 = 11. Here, we write down 1 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nSince there are no more digits, the carried-over 1 becomes the millions digit. So the total is 1 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 6 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 7 (ten), 8 (one). So the sum is 1,165,278.\n\nHmm, that seems right, but let me check using another method to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\n405,016 can be written as 400,000 + 5,000 + 16.\n\n760,262 is 700,000 + 60,000 + 200 + 62.\n\nAdding the large parts first:\n\n400,000 + 700,000 = 1,100,000.\n\nThen 5,000 + 60,000 = 65,000.\n\nNext, 200 + 16 + 62 = 200 + 78 = 278.\n\nAdding all those together: 1,100,000 + 65,000 = 1,165,000. Then add 278: 1,165,000 + 278 = 1,165,278. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. So the answer should be 1,165,278.\n</think>\n\n",
