\ufe0f\nHundreds: 4 +9 =13 \u2714\ufe0f, so 3 with carry 1\nThousands: 3 +1 +1 =5 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen-thousands:7+7=14 \u2714\ufe0f, so 4 with carry 1\nHundred-thousands:9+3+1=13 \u2714\ufe0f, so 3 with carry 1\nMillions: 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 1,345,386. Let me just add them using another method to cross-verify. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n973,437 + 371,949. Let's split into 900,000 + 73,437 and 300,000 + 71,949.\n\nAdding the large parts first: 900,000 + 300,000 = 1,200,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts: 73,437 + 71,949. Let's add those:\n\n73,437 + 70,000 = 143,437. Then add 1,949 more: 143,437 +1,949 = 145,386.\n\nNow add that to the 1,200,000: 1,200,000 + 145,386 = 1,345,386. Yep, same result. Okay, confident that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
