rried-over 1 from the previous step. So 8 + 1 = 9. That goes in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nPutting all the digits together, starting from the highest place to the lowest: 9 (hundred-thousands), 1 (ten-thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 6 (ones). So the total should be 916,886.\n\nWait a second, let me verify that again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them another way. Maybe breaking down the numbers:\n\n521,868 + 395,018.\n\nBreaking into parts:\n\n500,000 + 21,868\n\n+ 300,000 + 95,018\n\nAdding the large parts first: 500,000 + 300,000 = 800,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts: 21,868 + 95,018.\n\n21,868 + 95,018. Let's add those:\n\n21,868 + 95,018:\n\n21,868 + 95,000 = 116,868\n\nThen add the remaining 18: 116,868 + 18 = 116,886.\n\nNow add that to the 800,000: 800,000 + 116,886 = 916,886. Okay, that matches my previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method: adding column by column again.\n\nStarting over:\n\nNumbers:\n\n  521,868\n\n+395,018\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 +8 =16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 6 +1 =7 +1 (carryover) =8. So 8, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:8 +0=8.\n\nThousands:1 +5=6.\n\nTen-thousands:2 +9=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:5 +3=8 +1 (carryover)=9.\n\nSo the total is 916,886. Yep, same as before. I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes here. So the answer should be 916,886.\n</think>\n\n",
