e step by step to confirm:\n\nStarting over:\n\n315,756  \n+701,235  \n=?\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes: 6 +5 =11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1  \nTens:5+3 +1=9 \u2192 no carryover  \nHundreds:7+2=9  \nThousands:5+1=6  \nTen-thousands:1+0=1  \nHundred-thousands:3+7=10 \u2192 write 0 here, carryover 1 to millions place.  \nMillions place: the carried over 1. \n\nSo putting it all together: 1 (millions), 0 (hundred-thousands), 1 (ten-thousands), 6 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, that would be 1,016,991? Let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n315,756 + 701,235. Let's break them down:\n\n300,000 + 700,000 = 1,000,000  \n15,000 + 1,000 = 16,000  \n700 + 200 = 900  \n50 + 30 = 80  \n6 +5 =11. \n\nAdding those parts together: 1,000,000 +16,000 = 1,016,000; plus 900 is 1,016,900; plus 80 is 1,016,980; plus 11 is 1,016,991. Okay, that matches. So the correct sum is 1,016,991. \n\nI think my initial mistake was not considering the carryover into the millions place. So the final answer should be 1,016,991.\n</think>\n\n",
