 let me verify that again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait, let me add them another way to cross-check. Maybe breaking down the numbers:\n\n674,615 + 738,524.\n\nLet's split into parts:\n\n600,000 + 700,000 = 1,300,000\n\n70,000 + 30,000 = 100,000\n\n4,000 + 8,000 = 12,000\n\n600 + 500 = 1,100\n\n10 + 20 = 30\n\n5 +4 =9\n\nAdding all those parts together:\n\n1,300,000 + 100,000 = 1,400,000\n\n1,400,000 +12,000 = 1,412,000\n\n1,412,000 +1,100 = 1,413,100\n\n1,413,100 +30 = 1,413,130\n\n1,413,130 +9 =1,413,139. Okay, same result. That seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method. Let me add the numbers digit by digit again step by step to confirm.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5 +4 =9\n\nTens:1+2=3\n\nHundreds:6+5=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nThousands:4+8=12 +1=13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\nTen thousands:7+3=10 +1=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nHundred thousands:6+7=13 +1=14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\nMillions: the carried 1.\n\nSo the number is 1 (million), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (ones). So 1,413,139. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nHmm, I think that's correct. Let me try using another approach, perhaps adding the numbers as they are:\n\n674,615\n\n+738,524\n\nLet me add the units:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +4 =9 (ones)\n\n1 +2 =3 (tens)\n\n6 +5 =11 (hundreds, so 1 and carryover 1)\n\n4 (thousands) +8 (thousands) =12 thousands, plus 1 is 13. So 3 thousands, carryover 1.\n\n7 (ten thousands) +3 (ten thousands) =10 ten thousands, plus 1 is 11 ten thousands. So 1 ten thousand, carryover 1.\n\n6 (hundred thousands) +7 (hundred thousands) =13 hundred thousands, plus 1 is 14 hundred thousands. So 4 hundred thousands, carryover 1.\n\nThat gives the 1 in the millions place. So total is 1,413,139. \n\nI think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. So the final answer should be 1,413,139.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 674615 and 738524?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's add the