:\n\nNumbers are:\n  553,951\n+516,536\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 1 + 6 = 7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 5 + 3 = 8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 9 + 5 = 14. Write 4, carry 1. \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 3 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 9, plus the 1 carried over is 10. So write 0, carry 1. \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 5 (first number's ten-thousands digit) + 1 (second number's ten-thousands digit) = 6, plus the carried 1 makes 7. \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 (first number) + 5 (second number) = 10. So write 0 here and carry 1. Then the million's place is the carried 1. \n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 0 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 7 (ones). That's 1,070,487. Hmm, that seems right. Let me add them using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 553,951 + 516,536:\n\nBreak it down:\n\n500,000 + 500,000 = 1,000,000\n\n53,000 + 16,000 = 69,000 \u2192 total so far 1,069,000\n\n951 + 536 = 1,487 \u2192 total is 1,069,000 + 1,487 = 1,070,487. \n\nYes, that matches. Okay, so the answer should be correct.\n</think>\n\n",
