 + 9 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11, write 1, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nThousands: 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16, write 6, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen-thousands: 2 + 9 = 11 +1 =12, write 2, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundred-thousands: 3 +6 =9 +1=10, so write 0 and carry 1. Then the final 1 in the millions place. \n\nSo the sum is 1,026,142. Hmm, that seems right. Let me add them using another method to confirm. Maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n328,160 + 697,982. Let's split into 300,000 + 28,160 and 600,000 + 97,982. Adding the large parts: 300k + 600k = 900k. Then 28,160 + 97,982. \n\n28,160 + 97,982: 28k +97k is 125k, and 160 +982 is 1,142. So total 125,000 +1,142 =126,142. Then add to the 900k: 900k +126,142 = 1,026,142. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out.\n</think>\n\n",
