ethod like expanded form.\n\n500,960 can be written as 500,000 + 960.\n\n313,819 is 300,000 + 13,000 + 800 + 19.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n500,000 + 300,000 = 800,000\n\n13,000 + 0 (since 500,960 has no thousands) =13,000\n\n800 + 900 (from 960) = 1,700\n\n19 + 60 (remaining part of 960) =79\n\nWait, maybe this approach is getting confusing. Alternatively, adding 500,960 + 313,819:\n\nLet me add 500,000 + 300,000 = 800,000\n\nThen 0 (since 500,960 has 0 in the ten thousands place) +10,000 (from 313,819's 1 in the ten thousands place) =10,000 \u2192 total so far 810,000.\n\nThen 0 (thousands place in first number) + 3,000 (from 313,819's 3 in thousands place) =3,000 \u2192 total 813,000.\n\nThen 900 (from 500,960's hundreds place) + 800 (from 313,819's hundreds) =1,700 \u2192 adding to 813,000 gives 814,700.\n\nThen 60 (from 500,960's tens) +10 (from 313,819's tens place is 1, so 10) \u2192 70. Adding to 814,700 gives 814,770.\n\nFinally, the ones place: 0 +9 =9. So total is 814,779. Yep, matches the previous result. Okay, that seems correct. I think the answer is 814,779.\n</think>\n\n",
