s, 5 hundreds, 5 tens, 4 ones.\n\n354,531 is 3 hundred thousands, 5 ten thousands, 4 thousands, 5 hundreds, 3 tens, 1 one.\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 4+1=5 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:5+3=8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:5+5=10, so 0 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 3 +4 =7 plus the 1 carried over is 8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 0 +5 =5 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands:6+3=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the sum is indeed 958,085. I think that's correct. Let me just add the numbers another way to confirm. Maybe using another method like expanded form.\n\n603,554 can be written as 600,000 + 3,554.\n\n354,531 is 350,000 + 4,531.\n\nAdding the larger parts first: 600,000 + 350,000 = 950,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts: 3,554 + 4,531. Let's add those:\n\n3,554 + 4,531:\n\nThousands: 3,000 +4,000 =7,000\n\nHundreds: 500 +500 =1,000 \u2192 total so far 8,000\n\nTens:50 +30 =80\n\nOnes:4 +1=5\n\nAdding those: 8,000 +80 +5 =8,085.\n\nNow add that to the 950,000: 950,000 +8,085 =958,085. Yep, same result. Okay, that confirms it. The answer should be 958,085.\n</think>\n\n",
