 it's the hundred thousands place, adding 7 and 8 gives 15, so the hundred thousands digit becomes 5, and we carryover 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the millions digit. So the total is 1,546,463.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers again to check:\n\n743,486\n\n+802,977\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6+7=13 \u2192 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 8+7=15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:4+9=13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1.\n\nThousands:3+2=5 +1=6 \u21926, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:4+0=4 \u21924.\n\nHundred thousands:7+8=15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nMillions place: the carryover 1. So the total is 1,546,463.\n\nHmm, that seems right. Let me confirm by adding another way, maybe breaking down the numbers.\n\nAlternatively, 743,486 + 802,977.\n\nLet me add the thousands first. 743,486 is 743 thousands and 486. 802,977 is 802 thousands and 977. So adding the thousands: 743 + 802 = 1,545 thousands. Then adding the remaining parts: 486 + 977 = 1,463. So total is 1,545,000 + 1,463 = 1,546,463. Yep, same result. So that checks out. Okay, so the answer should be 1,546,463.\n</think>\n\n",
