housands place in 575,003 is the 7 in 575, so that's the 7 in the ten thousands place. The second number's ten thousands digit is 1 (from 115,267). So 7 +1 =8 plus the carried 1 makes 9. \n\nHundred thousands:5 +1=6. \n\nSo combining all digits: 6 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (ones). So 690,270. That seems right. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding 575,003 + 100,000 = 675,003. Then add 15,267. 675,003 +15,000 is 690,003. Then add 267: 690,003 +267 = 690,270. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
