fully.\n\nStarting over:\n\n**Ones place:** 9 + 2 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\n**Tens place:** 8 + 8 = 16, plus the 1 carried over is 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\n**Hundreds place:** 1 + 1 = 2, plus the 1 carried over is 3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\n**Thousands place:** 8 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 15. No carryover from hundreds, so 15. Wait, that's two digits. So write down 5 and carryover 1.\n\nAh, here's where I messed up earlier. The thousands place digits add to 15, so we have to carry over again.\n\n**Ten thousands place:** 2 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. So write 2 and carryover 1.\n\n**Hundred thousands place:** 3 + 6 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So write 0 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that 1 is added as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1\n\nTens:7\n\nHundreds:3\n\nThousands:5 (with a carryover 1)\n\nTen thousands: 2 (with a carryover 1)\n\nHundred thousands: 0 (with a carryover 1)\n\nAnd the final carryover 1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo the total would be 1,025,371?\n\nWait, let me verify that step by step again to be sure.\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\n328,189\n\n+697,182\n\nLet me add each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 9 + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carryover 1\n\nTens: 8 + 8 = 16 +1 =17 \u21927, carryover1\n\nHundreds:1 +1 =2 +1=3 \u21923, no carryover\n\nThousands:8 +7 =15 \u21925, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:2 +9 =11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:3 +6 =9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nMillions place: the carryover 1.\n\nSo putting all digits together: 1 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand),5 (thousand), 3 (hundred),7 (ten),1 (one). So 1,025,371.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 328,189 + 697,182.\n\nLet me break them into smaller parts:\n\n328,189 + 600,00