ds:7+2+1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nTen-thousands:6+5+1=12 \u21922, carry1.\n\nHundred-thousands:3+6+1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nThen the final carryover 1 is added as a new digit at the million's place. So the total is 1,020,611? Wait, but let me add the numbers another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding them as whole numbers:\n\n367,613 + 652,998.\n\nLet me break it down:\n\n367,613 + 600,000 = 967,613\n\nThen add 52,998: 967,613 +50,000 = 1,017,613; then +2,998 = 1,020,611. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,020,611. Wait, but let me check once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n      3 6 7 6 1 3\n    + 6 5 2 9 9 8\n    ----------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3+8=11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 1+9=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:6+9=15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nThousands:7+2=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nTen-thousands:6+5=11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1.\n\nHundred-thousands:3+6=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nThen the final carryover 1 is added as the next digit. So the total is 1,020,611. Yes, that seems correct. I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\n",
