2. So we write 2 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits to the left, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting all the digits together, starting from the millions place: 1 (million), 2 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, let me check that again. Wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, let me write it out step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\nNumbers aligned:\n\n\u20037 9 0 7 8 6\n+4 8 6 0 9 4\n------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n6 + 4 = 10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 8 + 9 = 17 + 1 (carry) = 18 \u2192 8, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 0 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8 \u2192 8, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 0 + 6 = 6 \u2192 6, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 4 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo the total is 1 (million), 2 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones). So that's 1,276,880?\n\nWait, let me verify that. Let me add the numbers another way to cross-check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n790,786 + 486,094.\n\nLet me separate the numbers into their components:\n\n790,786 = 700,000 + 90,000 + 700 + 80 + 6\n\nWait, actually, 790,786 is 700,000 + 90,000 + 0,000 (wait, no, 790,786 is 7 (100,000) * 7? Wait, no, 790,786 is 700,000 + 90,000 + 0,000? Wait, breaking down:\n\n790,786:\n\n- 7 (hundred thousands) \u2192 700,000\n\n- 9 (ten thousands) \u2192 90,000\n\n- 0 (thousands) \u2192 0\n\n- 7 (hundreds) \u2192 700\n\n- 8 (tens) \u2192 80\n\n- 6 (ones) \u2192 6\n\nSo total is 700,000 + 90,000 + 0 + 700 + 80 +6 = 790,786.\n\nSimilarly, 486,094 is:\n\n4 (hundred thousands) \u2192 400,000\n\n8 