ce, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits we've calculated are 3 (ones), 3 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 9 (thousands), 2 (ten-thousands), 9 (hundred-thousands), and the carried-over 1 in the millions place. So the total should be 1,929,833.\n\nWait a second, let me double-check to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them again quickly:\n\n988,598  \n+941,235  \n= ?\n\nAdding the ones: 8+5=13 (carry 1)  \nTens: 9+3+1=13 (carry 1)  \nHundreds:5+2+1=8  \nThousands:8+1=9  \nTen-thousands:8+4=12 (carry 1)  \nHundred-thousands:9+9+1=19 (carry 1)  \nMillions: the carried 1.\n\nSo yes, that gives 1,929,833. Hmm, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\nAlternatively, 988,598 + 941,235 can be thought of as (900,000 + 88,598) + (900,000 + 41,235). Adding the millions first: 900k + 900k = 1,800,000. Then the remaining parts: 88,598 +41,235. Let's add those:\n\n88,598 +41,235:  \nAdding the thousands: 88,000 +41,000 = 129,000  \nThen the hundreds: 598 +235 = 833  \nSo total is 129,000 +833 = 129,833. \n\nAdding that to the 1,800,000 gives 1,929,833. Okay, that matches. So I think that's correct. Maybe I should also use another way, like column addition again but more carefully.\n\nWait, another way: Let's add 988,598 + 941,235. Let me write them again:\n\n  988598  \n+941235  \n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 +5 =13. Write 3, carry 1.  \nTens:9+3=12 +1=13. Write 3, carry1.  \nHundreds:5+2=7 +1=8. Write8.  \nThousands:8+1=9. Write9.  \nTen-thousands:8+4=12. Write2, carry1.  \nHundred-thousands:9+9=18 +1=19. Write9, carry1.  \nMillions:1. So total is 1,929,833. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
